url: "https://cospira-arch.github.io"
abstract: >
  Since birth, humanity has repeatedly encountered the unknown: the classmate
  one first spoke with, the people of a neighboring settlement, a different
  nation, and now, an AI possessing an intelligence unlike our own. This
  paper places these encounters on a single theoretical field and attempts
  to construct a general theory describing when "encounter" is established,
  through three conditions: Kaikō, Withdrawal, and Reconfiguration. Encounter
  with AI, in particular, is a rare case offering ongoing, observable,
  verifiable data, and this paper takes it as the primary axis for
  theory-construction, cross-referencing the author's Boundary OS, Boundary
  Stability Index, Negentropy Index, and Techno-Animist Ethics frameworks.
keywords:
  - boundary studies
  - human-AI interaction
  - AI ethics
  - object-oriented ontology
  - philosophy of encounter
  - techno-animism
  - first contact
